# Operator Login AuthPageFrame Guardrail

Full reference: `docs/guardrails/2026-07-15_operator-login-auth-page-frame-guardrail.md`

## Hard rule (ZERO-TOUCH)

**Do not modify `OperatorLogin.jsx` or weaken its AuthPageFrame contract test unless the user's message in the CURRENT turn explicitly names operator login / restaurant sign-in and describes exactly what to change.**

Authorized UI: dark `AuthPageFrame` + green gradient `styles.submitButton`.  
Forbidden without approval: PageShell / BrandLogo light shell, solid blue `#1d4ed8` Sign in, “Restaurant Sign In” PageHero redesign on `/operator/login`.

## Never implement without explicit user approval

- Rewriting `/operator/login` to match restaurants landing or other light pages
- Changing Sign in button color/style away from `styles.submitButton`
- Removing AuthPageFrame / anti-`#1d4ed8` assertions from `siteFooterNavigationContract.test.js`

## Before editing protected files

Output:

> **Per Operator Login AuthPageFrame guardrail: the proposed change will modify [names] and may alter the authorized `/operator/login` AuthPageFrame UI. Explicit approval required.**

Then stop until approved.

## Mandatory on every task completion

End every response with:

> ☐ OPERATOR LOGIN CERTIFICATION: AuthPageFrame operator login [unchanged | user-approved change].

Protected: `OperatorLogin.jsx`, `siteFooterNavigationContract.test.js` (AuthPageFrame assertions).
